A||||7||Santa Cruzer||Where do i connect the power cord from my amp?||||1||
Z||000000||Santa Cruzer||09-16-2001||12:03 PM||||the red cord witht he fuse in it where does it go on the motor? pics would be nice or just instructions.thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-16-2001||01:19 PM||||How big of an amp is it?  Where is it going?<BR>Your amp haw wires attached to it already?<P>The power wire(red) should go to the + battery post.  The other one(black) should go to the - post.  The smaller remote wire(usually blue) gets 12V when the stereo is on and should get hooked up to the "remote" wire on the head unit or a switched 12V source.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||09-16-2001||01:35 PM||||Assuming that you're mounting the amp somewhere inside the car... the best way I found to run the wire to the battery is to remove the center consol and under the computer are a few rubber plugs where harnesses would go through.  I used a wire clothes hanger and tied the wire to it and pulled it throughto the engine compartment.  Also, by where you ran the red wire through on the inside, there is a screw for the center console that you can attached the ground wire too.  If you put the amp behind the seat you can then run your remote wire under the the side of the center console to the radio.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||09-16-2001||03:35 PM||||Don't have your ground wire longer than about 18"!!! Don't wire the amp directly to the battery. Run the + wire to the + terminal, and ground the amp to the frame. I ran a re sheiled cable from the battery, and through a hole drilled in the firewall. Looks great, works perfectly. I went in just above the Drivers side Ecm connector. Lots of room, you won't cut anything if you slip with the drill. Just be careful1||||reg||7
Z||000004||prtzlboy||09-16-2001||04:05 PM||||diddo what mach10 said about the ground wire.  Make it as short as possible.  When you wire your positive to the battery, make sure your inline fuse is close to the battery, and not the amp.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||09-16-2001||05:11 PM||||Hey dude, it's pretty easy, I ran my power wire out through one of the rear grommets.  The Ground should be short.<P>SantaCruiser -- I am free next weekend, if you want bring it down I will do it all for ya here.  Msg me or chat here.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
